  "contracts": [
    "All key inputs are encoded by original ggml_quantize_chunk or are explicit original raw words.",
    "The source scalar dot rounds products to F32 then sums in F64; ReLU uses the source MAX(qk,0) semantics.",
    "Mask grouping is sequence modulo, with actual physical byte strides.",
    "The second native zero-mask graph supplies an independent score-domain oracle; successful nonfinite source results remain preserved.",
    "Primary fixture covers every native key decoder, exhaustive half mask words, half/bfloat keys excluding positive infinity and all F8 words.",
    "Zero dimensions and empty unsupported-key types are retained when the original kernel admits them.",
    "C/C++ and native builds remain outside the product; original MIT attribution is preserved."
  ]
